  "title": "Amundsen completes the Northwest Passage in Gjøa",
  "summary": "Roald Amundsen left Norway in the small ship Gjøa on 16 June 1903 with a crew of six. The expedition wintered twice at Gjøa Haven on King William Island and reached Nome, Alaska on 30 August 1906, completing the passage by sea. The Fram Museum calls Gjøa the first ship sailed through the entire Northwest Passage.",
